<title>UK: Dixon picks up Carnell for 13.4 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Dixon picks up Carnell for 13.4 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British vehicle retailer Dixon Motors Plc said on Tuesday said it was buying The Carnell Motor Group Ltd for 13.4 million stg.</p>
<p>It also plans to raise 17.6 million stg through a one-for-three rights issue at 235p per share to fund the purchase of the motorcycle and car retailer.</p>
<p>Dixon will pay 1.4 million stg in cash, 5.2 million in shares and 6.8 million in loan notes. It will also repay Carnell debt of 10.5 million.</p>
<p>The company also announced that it expected pre-tax profits of 4.0 million stg for the six months to June 30, 1997 compared with 2.3 million previously.</p>
<p>It forecast an interim dividend payment of not less than 2.5p per share from 2.0p last time.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
